# 2026-07-26 (quality-mgr, AICH-S5-QA-5): fixed on feature/pAI-s25-peer-authority-resolution
# @ 96377687 (PR #640, merge of fix/pAI-s25-local-findings @ 3265270e), independently confirmed
# by ruthless-boundary-qa. resolve_peer_authority extracted into new dedicated module
# crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health/peer_authority.rs; https_transport.rs no longer contains
# any recipient-routing logic; post_write_router.rs is the sole caller and imports from the new
# location. New AST guard test added (boundary_enforcement.rs::
# ai25_peer_authority_selection_is_not_owned_by_the_https_adapter) prevents regression. Top-level
# status remains "open" only because s23/s24/s26 forked before this fix and still carry the
# violation on their own not-yet-merged branches (cascade, not a defect in this diff).
